{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>He is the Elohim.</b> The meaning: this is the Elohim in truth, who has power and is faithful. The reason is because of the oath, for there is one who is faithful but has no power to fulfill his oath, and there is one who has power but is not faithful." "<b>Who keeps the covenant and the kindness to those who love Him.</b> There is none above them." "<b>And to those who keep His commandments.</b> After them. Or its meaning: those who love Him in heart are those who keep His commandments in speech and in deed." "<b>To a thousand generations.</b> He erred who said that in thirty-six thousand years the wheel of the constellations returns, for the superior ones are found in seventy years, and the meaning of 'a thousand' is without end."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:41.847553158Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}